 "steps": [
  {
   "part": "oxline",
   "say": "Liquid oxygen arrives from its tank at the oxidiser pump, and this insulated line carries the pressurised oxidiser from the pump to the injector head. A smaller branch feeds the gas generator."
  },
  {
   "part": "oxpump",
   "say": "The oxidiser pump is a centrifugal pump: a spinning impeller flings the liquid outward into the scroll-shaped housing and raises its pressure far above the chamber pressure."
  },
  {
   "part": "fuelpump",
   "say": "The fuel pump does the same job for the fuel. Both pumps are needed because the chamber pressure is too high for tank pressure alone to push propellant in."
  },
  {
   "part": "fuelline",
   "say": "The fuel line takes pressurised fuel up to the injector head. A branch of it goes to the gas generator, and in a real engine the main flow usually passes through the nozzle wall first."
  },
  {
   "part": "gg",
   "say": "The gas generator burns a small share of the propellant, with one of them in large excess, so the gas stays cool enough for the turbine blades. Its only job is to make hot gas that drives the turbines."
  },
  {
   "part": "ducts",
   "say": "The hot gas ducts carry the generator's output to the two turbines. After the turbines, the exhaust pipes vent it near the nozzle, which wastes a little performance but keeps the design simple."
  },
  {
   "part": "turbine",
   "say": "Each turbine housing guides the hot gas onto the turbine blades and collects it again on the way out."
  },
  {
   "part": "rotor",
   "say": "The gas spins the turbine wheel, and a shaft passes that rotation straight up into the pump. This loop is what powers the engine from its own propellant."
  },
  {
   "part": "gimbal",
   "say": "The gimbal mount joins the engine to the rocket frame on a ball joint. Actuators tilt the whole engine a few degrees to steer the thrust."
  },
  {
   "part": "head",
   "say": "The injector head is a manifold. It spreads fuel and oxidiser over the whole top of the chamber and holds the injector plate against the chamber flange."
  },
  {
   "part": "plate",
   "say": "The injector plate has a ring pattern of holes. Each jet sprays and mixes the two propellants so they burn evenly, and a fuel-rich layer at the chamber wall helps protect the metal."
  },
  {
   "part": "chamber",
   "say": "Propellants burn here at high pressure. The hot gas is squeezed through the narrowest part, the throat, where it reaches the speed of sound."
  },
  {
   "part": "nozzle",
   "say": "The bell nozzle lets the gas expand and speed up, turning heat into forward thrust. Tubes in the wall carry fuel that absorbs heat, so the metal survives, and the bands stiffen the thin wall."
  }
 ]
}